### Step 1 of 2: request an upload.
### Note the size: it is signed, so the file you PUT next must be exactly this many bytes.
POST http://localhost:8080/uploads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contentType": "image/png",
  "sizeBytes": 21,
  "filename": "cat.png"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("uploadUrl", response.body.upload.url);
    client.global.set("uploadId", response.body.uploadId);
    client.log("PUT the bytes to " + response.body.upload.url);
%}

### Step 2 of 2: send the bytes straight to S3. This never touches the API.
### If this 403s here but works in curl, add the line "# @no-auto-encoding" above the PUT:
### the IntelliJ HTTP Client percent-encodes request URLs by default, and the presigned URL is
### already encoded.
PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/png

pretend this is a png

### Negative case: the same URL with a different media type. Expect 403 SignatureDoesNotMatch.
PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

pretend this is a png

### Read the status back.
GET http://localhost:8080/images/{{uploadId}}
